{"id": "185836", "name": "02 - x(1,2,3)-y(3,2,1)", "qtype": "truefalse", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 1, "options": {}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\">\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ W = \\{x(1,2,3)-y(3,2,1) : x,y \\in \\mathbb{R} \\} \\]</p>\n<p>Is <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(W\\)</span> a subspace of <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\mathbb{R}^3\\)</span>?</p>\n</div>\n</div><div class=\"native-answer\">[[input:ans]]</div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> We check the three conditions: the zero vector, closure under addition, closure under scalar multiplication.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — W is a span</b><br><span dir=\"ltr\">\\(x(1,2,3)-y(3,2,1)=x(1,2,3)+(-y)(3,2,1)\\)</span>, and as <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(y\\)</span> runs over <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\mathbb{R}\\)</span> so does <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(-y\\)</span>. Hence<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ W=\\operatorname{span}\\{(1,2,3),(3,2,1)\\}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The three conditions</b><br>Zero: <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(x=y=0\\)</span>. Sum: <span dir=\"ltr\">\\([x_1(1,2,3)-y_1(3,2,1)]+[x_2(1,2,3)-y_2(3,2,1)]=(x_1+x_2)(1,2,3)-(y_1+y_2)(3,2,1)\\)</span>. Scalar: <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(\\lambda[x(1,2,3)-y(3,2,1)]=(\\lambda x)(1,2,3)-(\\lambda y)(3,2,1)\\)</span>. All of these have the required form, so <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(W\\)</span> is a subspace (every span is a subspace).\n<p style=\"text-align:center\"><b>The statement is true.</b></p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "[[feedback:prt1]]", "prtcorrect": "", "prtpartiallycorrect": "", "prtincorrect": "", "inputs": [{"name": "ans", "type": "radio", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": false, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": false, "showvalidation": 0, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "native": {"shuffle": false, "numbering": "none", "instruction": "one", "lang": "en"}}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "native": true, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": []}], "qvnames": [], "nvariants": 1}